{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes","id":1328407,"title":"[spoilers] Aberrant Setting Changes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-30T17:16:11-07:00","id":1328407,"title":"[spoilers] Aberrant Setting Changes","content":"So as a huge fan of Aberrant 1e, I devoured the manuscript docs as soon as they became available to me, especially the setting/history info, and found so many changes that really made me happy. Although I want to be sure about a couple things before I rejoice too much just in case that I missed it..<br /> <br /> Am I right that the whole &quot;nobles are sterile&quot; storyline has been dropped in 2e? Not a thing at all? Seems so to me, but want to confirm. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, let me say that T2N, what is going on with the Aberrants, etc.. really exciting stuff. Thrilled to see some significant setting work done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5930-deathchipmunk","name":"DeathChipmunk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T17:45:40-07:00","id":1328412,"title":"","content":"I'm still mulling it all over, but at first blush I agree with you. And yes, I think the birth control plot is gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T20:03:30-07:00","id":1328440,"title":"","content":"Eyup. Nothing in the entire book about a sterilization conspiracy. Additionally, Slider is breathing, and Proteus aren't mustache twirling villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T21:23:45-07:00","id":1328447,"title":"","content":"Yeah the sterilization plot is gone, and that is for the best. I want to turn up the shadows a bit at my own table, but I\u2019ll find other ways to morally compromise Utopia and co, because that plot line never worked if you thought about it too long.<br /> <br /> That said, I\u2019m houseruling a) all Novas are slow aging it\u2019s not an Edge you have to buy, b) Novas are as fertile as baselines RELATIVE TO NATIRAL LIFETIME, and c) this hasn\u2019t been conclusively figured out 10 years after N-Day, and there are starting to be concerns about Nova infertility, including untrue sterilization conspiracy theories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T22:38:56-07:00","id":1328461,"title":"","content":"One point the devs made in an interview was that, if someone finds out about the Medusa Protocols and makes that public, there\u2019s plenty of ammo there to indicate that Utopia is totally morally compromised, especially if you only get bits and pieces of the info. <br /> <br /> Someone who got some partial information off a deeply hidden Utopia server might even think that there actually WAS a sterilization plot or that Utopia was going to just kill all the Novas the moment they step out of line, instead of try to contain and then rehabilitate them.<br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019m inclined to think that one of the few things that might totally derail the Aberrant War, instead of just pushing it a few years into the future, is finding a way to help Burano invent Quantakinesis much, much earlier. That might actually help reduce Flux and even Transcendence, which could help keep Novas from going Aberrant, negate their powers, and might even end up with some kind of drug you could take to stop becoming a disinterested god.<br /> <br /> Granted Divis Mal probably wouldn\u2019t like it, but, honestly, he lost control of this situation about ten years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T04:11:26-07:00","id":1328488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathChipmunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes#post1328407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I right that the whole &quot;nobles are sterile&quot; storyline has been dropped in 2e? Not a thing at all? Seems so to me, but want to confirm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> By making the Aeon Society the good guys, that had a cascading effect on the setting:<br /> <br /> Aeon are good -&gt; no nova sterilization conspiracy -&gt; Slider doesn't get assassinated -&gt; Corbin and Rousseau don't form the Aberrants -&gt; T2N happens instead -&gt; Aberrants form as a sub-group of Teragen<br /> <br /> Deciding that the Fireman was going to be our first big example of Sacrifice was a second big change, but didn't have the same ripple effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T04:16:18-07:00","id":1328490,"title":"","content":"I want to play this game NOW!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T05:39:58-07:00","id":1328501,"title":"","content":"Also, a change that my buddy pointed out to me. There are actually a lot less Novas present at the start of 2e than the start of 1e. There is only like 2K novas, and that means there is less of a chance for them to breed. Thus it is harder to see if they are fertile or infertile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T06:55:11-07:00","id":1328508,"title":"","content":"This 2K novas in the world part is one thing that really matter, not on the breeding per se, but on the importance of our characters to the world and the importance of every single Elite.<br /> <br /> You may say 6k to 2K is not a big gap, but if you think how many of the novas are not heroic oriented, how many are not willing to risk their lives, how many of them are dark stars, how many just don\u2019t want to be novas, you cut the relevant novas to a few hundred, and the ones that are a serious risk to a few dozens, while we were talking about a thousand and a few hundreds before.<br /> <br /> Also you don\u2019t need to put Pax on Q6 or Mal at Q8 to make them the most powerful by 2028, but let\u2019s see how the Proteus files will make them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T07:08:51-07:00","id":1328509,"title":"","content":"The reduced number makes it feel even more like Rising Stars to me, which is good in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T08:32:05-07:00","id":1328538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1328509#post1328509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reduced number makes it feel even more like Rising Stars to me, which is good in my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rising Star it\u2019s a bit too far on the counting... but that\u2019s my point of view too.<br /> <br /> Actually my idea for a non-Aberrant-War future is more of a Rising Star, the novas rise in conflict between them and against humanity too, but the war don\u2019t end on the Ultimatum, it end with the novas uniting and helping humanity to create a better future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T09:34:36-07:00","id":1328558,"title":"","content":"I do think there\u2019s room for a loose equivalent of 1e Aberrant without the specific conspiracy to respond to. Think of Cap\u2019s side of Marvel Civil War and subsequent Secret Avengers. Some people are going to want to be heroes and fight against efforts to regulate them in that regard.<br /> <br /> Obviously T2N is kind of a response to this - they do the missions that T2M can\u2019t do because the Security Council wouldn\u2019t approve. But I don\u2019t just mean black ops for an official institution - I mean full on rejection of the restrictions of such an institution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T10:01:17-07:00","id":1328567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1328558#post1328558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obviously T2N is kind of a response to this - they do the missions that T2M can\u2019t do because the Security Council wouldn\u2019t approve. But I don\u2019t just mean black ops for an official institution - I mean full on rejection of the restrictions of such an institution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did enjoy them as an addition. It meant there was now a Utopia/Aeon faction I could actually get onboard with. Bhurano being around means there would be another Aeon affiliate I can side with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T10:49:15-07:00","id":1328575,"title":"","content":"Bhurano is not affiliated to Aeon, she is working by herself for a while and may be related to a few people inside, but she is not part of it. Yet she is one of the most capable scientists in the subject of Noetic and Quantum by the time and could be behind of a group of dark stars and psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T14:08:49-07:00","id":1328610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1328575#post1328575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bhurano is not affiliated to Aeon, she is working by herself for a while and may be related to a few people inside, but she is not part of it. Yet she is one of the most capable scientists in the subject of Noetic and Quantum by the time and could be behind of a group of dark stars and psiads.</div> </div> </div> </div>From context, I assume Darksol was confusing her with fellow Psiad Sophia Rosseau.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T14:45:24-07:00","id":1328612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1328610#post1328610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From context, I assume Darksol was confusing her with fellow Psiad Sophia Rosseau.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, make sense... Rousseau is one of those interesting characters that I never used on my stories but would like to... I don't know why I didn't, I guess I never used much of conspiracy on my games and she is basically a walking urban legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T14:57:05-07:00","id":1328615,"title":"","content":"A question I think Ian is the only source to go.<br /> <br /> In 1e pre-N-Day aberrants were treated as urban legends by 2008, but Aeon didn't let this information go public (they were fully aware of Stalwarts and knew most of the Pre-N-Day Novas). I mean, Fireman was know as the first Nova eruption, not the first nova gone public or the first that was reported. Pax for example would deny that he erupted before N-Day but there were rumours that he did.<br /> <br /> In this new &quot;Good Guys Aeon&quot; what's the politics about the public knowledge of pre-N-Day? Does the general population know Pax was a nova for 40 years before Fireman erupted? I guess they know lotto to nothing about Mal and Scripture, but what about other Novas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T15:08:53-07:00","id":1328619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1328615#post1328615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question I think Ian is the only source to go.<br /> <br /> In 1e pre-N-Day aberrants were treated as urban legends by 2008, but Aeon didn't let this information go public (they were fully aware of Stalwarts and knew most of the Pre-N-Day Novas). I mean, Fireman was know as the first Nova eruption, not the first nova gone public or the first that was reported. Pax for example would deny that he erupted before N-Day but there were rumours that he did.<br /> <br /> In this new &quot;Good Guys Aeon&quot; what's the politics about the public knowledge of pre-N-Day? Does the general population know Pax was a nova for 40 years before Fireman erupted? I guess they know lotto to nothing about Mal and Scripture, but what about other Novas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they regurarly mistake psiads for novas, so the general knowledge of these things, even on high levels seems to be pretty much zilch. More serious answer i expect. Leave it to GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T15:17:24-07:00","id":1328622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1328615#post1328615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this new &amp;quot;Good Guys Aeon&amp;quot; what's the politics about the public knowledge of pre-N-Day? Does the general population know Pax was a nova for 40 years before Fireman erupted? I guess they know lotto to nothing about Mal and Scripture, but what about other Novas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Public don\u2019t know anything. N-day was when it all started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T15:29:12-07:00","id":1328625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1328622#post1328622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Public don\u2019t know anything. N-day was when it all started.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I was thinking, it's far more interesting for investigating the past.<br /> <br /> Two more questions related.<br /> <br /> Does Aeon deny the pre-N-Day novas or is there a &quot;we never met one&quot; / &quot;if there was never showed up&quot; escuse?<br /> <br /> Is there a rumour among the great media or just conspiracy theories?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T15:55:02-07:00","id":1328633,"title":"","content":"As a related question are we the only ones that know that Divis Mal is Dr Primoris is Michael Donigal or do some people in the world itself know of the connection. (I don't mean Scripture, as I assume Divis Mal told his lover of his past.) Like does Aeon know its the same person despite different names.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the fact that Novas existed pre-N Day means to me there should have been a nova politican or business leader. Someone with access to quantum abilities, even if it was just non-flashy Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges, who acted to make his company or state better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T16:28:06-07:00","id":1328640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1328610#post1328610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From context, I assume Darksol was confusing her with fellow Psiad Sophia Rosseau.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I was referring to Proxy Bhurano, not Sophia. I just assumed that she'd be lurking in Aeon's records and library under some assumed identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T16:28:07-07:00","id":1328641,"title":"","content":"For sure there is some guys from Aeon that knew Mal from his previous lives (before the first Chrysalis) but how much did he changed since then? For sure the Aeon council went after his origins when he published and probably found something, enough to go after the living last few from old Aeon Society of Gentleman members. Thats my guess at least.<br /> On 1e its said that he physically changed a lot between he left Aeon Society and they faced him later, to the point some of the former team mates didn't recognised him at first, and he didn't had his first Chrysalis yet.<br /> <br /> Also there are more than just Mal and Scripture that were Terats before N-Day, I guess at least, and I think there was some of them that also know his origin even without knowing from before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T16:33:40-07:00","id":1328642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1328640#post1328640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I was referring to Proxy Bhurano, not Sophia. I just assumed that she'd be lurking in Aeon's records and library under some assumed identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not impossible, but on Aberrant last chapter she is said to be under the name Krona Bush and working for herself and possibly working with other psiads and maybe novas and talents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T16:34:32-07:00","id":1328643,"title":"","content":"Back in 1e Mathematician was another pre N-day eruptee, not that he's likely to spread that around. And the 1e Aberrants used to have a Novox singer who erupted from 103 back into youth who would know Divis Mal for Dr. Primoris by virtue of living in that era. Not that I' ve heard any mention of her mind you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T16:42:28-07:00","id":1328645,"title":"","content":"After we get Adventure! I\u2019m inclined to make pre-N-Day Pax a powerful Stalwart rather than a full blown Nova.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d treat Primoris as a powerful Stalwart until 1945 - have him go into Chrysalis from which he emerges as the first modern Nova after the Trinity blast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T16:56:58-07:00","id":1328647,"title":"","content":"Personally I would make Stalwarts Novas limited to Q2 and build with about 60XP, that's about how much experience you gain as a new Talent.<br /> <br /> But so far I am really waiting to see Psiads from Aexpansion before try to balance Stalwarts to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T17:21:13-07:00","id":1328648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1328647#post1328647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would make Stalwarts Novas limited to Q2 and build with about 60XP, that's about how much experience you gain as a new Talent.<br /> <br /> But so far I am really waiting to see Psiads from Aexpansion before try to balance Stalwarts to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psiads don\u2019t balance with Stalwarts. Mesmerists do. At least in 1e, and I assume it will be the same this time since putting Mode mechanics, even at lower levels, for Adventure! PCs would be genre-breakingly powerful - so Mesmerists require separate mechanics and Stalwarts are mechanically alongside those, not Psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T18:09:31-07:00","id":1328651,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the scale system kept the low quantum novas pretty weak, compared to the old Mega Atributes and unlimited dots in the powers once the quantum minimum is reached.<br /> <br /> For example, Mega Speed 1 make you capable a hold the speed of an athlete for an entire marathon, probably finishing it in under an hour, it's on pulp range. Mega Might allow you to lift 3 or 4 times the usual limit of your strength, its far from a ton unless you are a professional weight lifting athlete, very pulp too.<br /> <br /> Another thing that I must bring is the fact that Talents and Psions can work together with no issue in Aeon, and its possible to add a talent on Aberrant and still don't miss much of the game. Unless you are planning to add Dramatic Edition to the Stalwart and Mesmerist reach (what don't sound interesting from the &quot;each kind have their own powers&quot;) you don't need to remove any of the Q2 powers (maybe shrink, this power is too effective for a low quantum character) to keep it Pulp-ish.<br /> <br /> A few Dynamic Knacks that were not very Pulp-ish in Adventure and still are there (not even touching the Psychic power): Single Bound (lvl 1: 3 times distance and hight jump), Man of all seasons (lvl 1: -30 to 150 C without risks), Blazing Speed (2: entire extra action in the round), Body of Bronze (3: you turn into metal), Man of Many Faces (3: you can change your aparente), Reptilian Regeneration (3: recover lost body parts).<br /> <br /> My players, when we anted something really pulp, used to use only Deredevils, because Mesmerists and Stalwarts were a bit out of the genre we desired.<br /> <br /> Well, that's my opinion, I always wanted to make a cross from Adventure to Aberrant without changing character sheets, but it was never possible. I hope they keep the possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T19:31:40-07:00","id":1328658,"title":"","content":"Look its clear that to you Stalwarts are just Novas with a lower Quantum score and lesser powers, but from what we know from First Edition and conversations from the new one, that is not what they are. Stalwarts (Superiors), Mesmerists, and Daredevils (Talents) are of a lower order of Inspired. They are their own thing. They are powerful yes, but they are not at the same category as the greater ones; with them being Novas (naturally formed quantum users) and Psiads (naturally formed noetic users). <br /> <br /> This is from someone who likes the idea of the potential that an Inspiration 10 Stalwart could become a full on Nova and an Inspiration 10 Mesmerist could become a Psi 2 Psiad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T00:43:04-07:00","id":1328901,"title":"","content":"I notice that more Talents are sprinkled here and there in the new canon, like Alexi Zhukov being an actual Talent as opposed to <i>merely</i> a vicious KGB vet. I don't think I saw Petr Ilyanovich of the Directive being upgraded past baseline though so looks like he'll be even more frustrated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T12:31:52-07:00","id":1328998,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going to make a post with my setting tweaks and expansions. Among them, I\u2019m adding two major Allegiances that form a quadrant chart without Utopia and Teragen along the axes of \u201cidentify as human\u201d and \u201cindividualist vs collectivist\u201d. So there will be a major faction for individualist Novas who identify as human, and collectivist Novas who do not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-03-2019, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-04T09:53:41-07:00","id":1329301,"title":"","content":"So I can't help but wonder what Aberrant would be like if say the start date was 2019, that is, novas appeared in October 2018 but its only been a year since then. The players are the first crop of novas to fully manifest. Which means they get to be on the ground initiating events that come later. <br /> <br /> I could totally see keeping the timeline events continuing in areas that players don't touch. (So if no player is about terraforming then Utopia still cleans the environment, and if no player is about medicine than Triton still creates cures.) But I could see making major changes based on the areas the players impact. <br /> <br /> Honestly, while I don't hate the timeline I do think its not as changed as it should / could be considering ten years of nova presence. <br /> <br /> I do wonder if others have ideas on additional timeline points or moments they would want to add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-04T12:02:21-07:00","id":1329312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1329301#post1329301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I can't help but wonder what Aberrant would be like if say the start date was 2019, that is, novas appeared in October 2018 but its only been a year since then. The players are the first crop of novas to fully manifest. Which means they get to be on the ground initiating events that come later. <br /> <br /> I could totally see keeping the timeline events continuing in areas that players don't touch. (So if no player is about terraforming then Utopia still cleans the environment, and if no player is about medicine than Triton still creates cures.) But I could see making major changes based on the areas the players impact. <br /> <br /> Honestly, while I don't hate the timeline I do think its not as changed as it should / could be considering ten years of nova presence. <br /> <br /> I do wonder if others have ideas on additional timeline points or moments they would want to add.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* Day one eruptee is a pretty common game concept. It can be fun. Done it at least once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-04T13:29:55-07:00","id":1329322,"title":"","content":"Right, but to play out being there from the beginning means that actions have to matter and that those actions could lead to other changes in the world. Player developed technology and player created political movements, etc. <br /> <br /> A player building a company. A player pushing the election. Players hacking into some sort of information system and releasing political news to the world. From that I think lots and lots of changes would happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-04T17:53:18-07:00","id":1329359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1329322#post1329322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but to play out being there from the beginning means that actions have to matter and that those actions could lead to other changes in the world. Player developed technology and player created political movements, etc.<br /> <br /> A player building a company. A player pushing the election. Players hacking into some sort of information system and releasing political news to the world. From that I think lots and lots of changes would happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they would. They always did. I mean, unless the GM's got a bug up his butt for the official timeline and railroads it into existence, but then there's no point in playing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-04T20:59:45-07:00","id":1329380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1329301#post1329301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I can't help but wonder what Aberrant would be like if say the start date was 2019, that is, novas appeared in October 2018 but its only been a year since then. The players are the first crop of novas to fully manifest. Which means they get to be on the ground initiating events that come later.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is another thread in this forum titled &quot;What if Galatea happened today&quot; that explores what you're talking about to some degree. I'd link it here if I knew how.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I rather like the setting changes thus far, they'll make an excellent framework when I do exactly what we're talking about and have my first set of PCs be 1st-wave eruptees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-05T12:24:00-07:00","id":1329477,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m considering tying N-Day to the activation of CERN LHC in 2008, and placing the setting \u201cnow\u201d in a divergent present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-05T13:33:21-07:00","id":1329486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1329477#post1329477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m considering tying N-Day to the activation of CERN LHC in 2008, and placing the setting \u201cnow\u201d in a divergent present.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about it a few times, but more about the CERN LHC working for all the 3 not just Novas. More like a Telluric Engine than a Galetea. But the idea is great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-05T19:08:59-07:00","id":1329554,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if the world could handle Novas, Psiads, and super-Talents all appearing at the same time. Hehe<br /> <br /> It would be awesome though. All the fun that could be had with humanity being enhanced in such an advanced way. <br /> <br /> As a note, I always thought it would be interesting if in the near future humanity goes to space and as we do the Inspired start to manifest. But that is not so much N-Day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T13:28:36-07:00","id":1329959,"title":"","content":"You know what I would really like, a Trinity setting where it is the Inspired who are the ones that head into space and organize humanity's future. <br /> <br /> In 'simple' terms the Expanse but with Inspired. hehe<br /> <br /> Or more organized, humanity has expanded within the solar system to the point that there are bases, outposts, colonies, and or stations on every main world, their major moons, and a vast assortment of asteroids. This would be a humanity that has a UN like structure for high level diplomacy (which could be a fun game structure) but numerous individual planetary nations competing within themselves and with each other. <br /> <br /> I could even see keeping the whole Nova Age and Aberrant War. Basically novas appeared like canon and thanks to their work numerous colonies throughout the solar system were established and their worlds terraformed somewhat. Things happened, events heated up, and the Aberrant War occurred that drove them from the solar system.Maybe the act that saw the novas leave also caused a wave of energy to engulf the solar system, one like the Hammersmith Event. Due to this wave came a second Adventure! era where Stalwarts, Mesmersits, and Talents were present in high quantities (plus the occasional stealth Nova and hidden Psiad).<br /> <br /> Maybe Divis Mals' final act of aid to humanity before he departed for elsewhere was to protect the Sol System in a barrier of energy. A sphere that due to certain actions in the present of the timeline will soon come down and lead to the potential expansion of humanity among the stars. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T03:51:46-07:00","id":1330906,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a really interesting idea for a Setting! This combination of &quot;Expanse&quot; and a new, second era Adventure! reminds me somewhat about Allen Steeles Captain-Future-Reboot &quot;Avengers of the Moon&quot;. (<a href=\"https://books.google.de/books/about/Avengers_of_the_Moon.html?id=w5RODgAAQBAJ&amp;source=kp_book_description&amp;redir_esc=y\" target=\"_blank\">https://books.google.de/books/about/...on&amp;redir_esc=y</a>). This also combines relatively &quot;hard&quot; modern Space-Opera with the pulpy, adventurous Sci-Fi of old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24955,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","user":"Waldi","date":". 08-14-2019, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T14:48:50-07:00","id":1331868,"title":"","content":"Reading over this thread, I see a lot of references I don't get... Is it possible to play Aberrant without being very familiar with the Aeon setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I am a prophet. I bring chaos and unrest to the foolish and wicked. I am no fit prince for Cainites, and I am no fit shepherd for the souls of men.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24720-anatole","name":"Anatole","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T14:57:46-07:00","id":1331870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anatole</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1331868#post1331868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading over this thread, I see a lot of references I don't get... Is it possible to play Aberrant without being very familiar with the Aeon setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, actually it doesn't cause any issue and some SG would even prefer players that don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T15:04:36-07:00","id":1331873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anatole</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1331868#post1331868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading over this thread, I see a lot of references I don't get... Is it possible to play Aberrant without being very familiar with the Aeon setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, how they tie together is really only relevant from the Aeon side since Aberrant is its past, but if you\u2019re playing Aberrant Aeon does not have to be its future.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll even point out that the go-to example of pulpy stuff like Gorilla City existing in the Adventure! era but going out-of-Phase with the timeline that continues to Aberrant and Aeon means that completely different alien civilizations might exist out there in the Aberrant era as befits comic book super heroics, as opposed to the COMPARATIVELY harder sci-fi aliens of the Aeon setting. So you really don\u2019t need to worry about Aeon to play Aberrant.<br /> <br /> The main thing Aeon can contribute Aberrant is better rules for Psiads, but that\u2019s not necessary at all if you aren\u2019t specifically interested in playing psychic characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T15:33:55-07:00","id":1331877,"title":"","content":"I only ever encountered Aberrant 1e, so while I knew about the (broad) metaplot connections to Aeon and Adventure!, I never really knew the details. I didn't think there were psionic characters in Aberrant 1e and I have no idea what a Stalwart is/was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I am a prophet. I bring chaos and unrest to the foolish and wicked. I am no fit prince for Cainites, and I am no fit shepherd for the souls of men.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24720-anatole","name":"Anatole","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T16:07:53-07:00","id":1331881,"title":"","content":"Stalwarts are the proto-novas, as they were in Adventure Era, much weaker than the Novas, but still basically quantum powered. There were also in the Adventure Era the Mesmerists (proto-Psions) and the Daredevils (extremely lucky or talented \u201cnormal\u201d people)<br /> <br /> There was Psiads (natural manifested Psions) in Aberrant era 1e, and you find rules for them in Aberrant Players Guide. They were seen as Novas, but they were \u201cinvisible\u201d to Node background and had no node at all. As there were no more than a few dozen and over 6k nova s in 2008, nobody cared about them, only exception is Aeon Society that had a Project just for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-20-2019, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T01:34:24-07:00","id":1331926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anatole</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1331868#post1331868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading over this thread, I see a lot of references I don't get... Is it possible to play Aberrant without being very familiar with the Aeon setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you\u2019d probably need to read Aberrant itself and not just this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T19:20:44-07:00","id":1332055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1331881#post1331881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stalwarts are the proto-novas, as they were in Adventure Era, much weaker than the Novas, but still basically quantum powered. There were also in the Adventure Era the Mesmerists (proto-Psions) and the Daredevils (extremely lucky or talented \u201cnormal\u201d people)</div> </div> </div> </div>Daredevils would probably use the rules for Talents, but could Stalwarts and Mesmerists be played in the Aberrant and Aeon eras, or are they no longer created with the fading of the Hammersmith Explosion?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T20:08:22-07:00","id":1332058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332055#post1332055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Daredevils would probably use the rules for Talents, but could Stalwarts and Mesmerists be played in the Aberrant and Aeon eras, or are they no longer created with the fading of the Hammersmith Explosion?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that falls under the Continuum principle of tailoring the specifics being mutually viable differentiations in timeline. Certainly the 2e Adventure! rules should function well enough.<br /> <br /> I think the setting\u2019s default assumption though is that Mesmerists evolved in Psiads in future eras and I\u2019m not sure what having both Psiads and Mesmerists around at the same time would add to anything. There being room for natural occurring Tier Two counterparts to Novas could be interesting though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T22:26:48-07:00","id":1332069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332058#post1332058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the setting\u2019s default assumption though is that Mesmerists evolved in Psiads in future eras and I\u2019m not sure what having both Psiads and Mesmerists around at the same time would add to anything. There being room for natural occurring Tier Two counterparts to Novas could be interesting though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Would Psiads be only post-Galatea, or would they be in the modern age of the Core book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T22:34:57-07:00","id":1332072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332069#post1332069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would Psiads be only post-Galatea, or would they be in the modern age of the Core book?</div> </div> </div> </div>N-day was pretty much tailor made to make novas. Psiads would realistically be roughly just as common before as after it, I imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T22:36:36-07:00","id":1332073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332069#post1332069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would Psiads be only post-Galatea, or would they be in the modern age of the Core book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Storyguide call. If they exist they\u2019d be exceptionally rare (same post-N-Day honestly), but we know pre-N-Day Novas exist, so I see no reason why that couldn\u2019t be possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T01:51:33-07:00","id":1332092,"title":"","content":"Psiads have been around since at least the Hammersmith incident*. Bhurano was the most powerful (much like Michael and Max were the most powerful of their type) but they were pre-Galatea.<br /> <br /> * Since the Hammersmith explosion echoed back and forwards in time (in 1st edition, at least), from the moment of the explosion psiads were around before it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T03:18:12-07:00","id":1332097,"title":"","content":"Stalwarts and Psiads were around since as long as needed, from gods and wizard to pulp heroes, the point is, they were few and had limited power, so their impact on history became almost nothing, or no more than legends.<br /> <br /> Stalwarts could always evolve to Novas, but Mal was probably the first to, and it happened just because of the Hammersmith accident, that give him that little push.<br /> <br /> Also, Bunyip basically said Mesmerists are Psiads, that made my day...<br /> <br /> Edit: must explain the Mesmerist Psiad thing. I have in mind that Mesmerists are Psiads and others keep saying they are not, they are weaker then Psiads.<br /> I also think that Stalwarts are just low Quantum Novas, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-22-2019, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T05:06:26-07:00","id":1332102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332097#post1332097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Bunyip basically said Mesmerists are Psiads, that made my day...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332097#post1332097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: must explain the Mesmerist Psiad thing. I have in mind that Mesmerists are Psiads and others keep saying they are not, they are weaker then Psiads.<br /> I also think that Stalwarts are just low Quantum Novas, by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, you are 100% wrong about Mesmerists = Psiads *and* Stalwarts = low Quantum novas. Both were like flawed proto-versions of novas and psiads, plucking the odd individual powers from areas but lacking the fully fleshed out power sets the others had. Now maybe, just maybe, a second Hammersmith-like event tuned towards Quantum could boost Stalwarts over the line and let them mini-erupt into nova status, and maybe the same could occur with Mesmerists, a psi-themed event, and psiads.<br /> <br /> Nothing has been set down for 2e yet, so who knows what might happen.<br /> <br /> But at least one nova (and probably more) and one psiad (and probably more) existed around the time of the Hammersmith event. When the world turned to pulp-adventure and Stalwarts and Mesmerists came to the fore alongside Daredevils, these novas and psiads probably either looked on them with amusement, or thought themselves the same but wondered why the others were so incredibly limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 08-22-2019, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T05:38:37-07:00","id":1332109,"title":"","content":"A Stalwart is a limited Quantum user and a Mesmerist is a limited Psi user. So you mean a Stalwart cannot train to became a Nova and a Mesmerist cannot train became a Psiad?<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s have 3 Psi users, Psiad, Psion and Proxy. A psiad can never became a Psion because of the way you became a Psion, same way a Psion cannot became a Proxy, but a psiad can be as powerful as a Psion (and virtually, if not blocked on Aexpansion) as powerful as a Proxy. But a Psion can train and became a tier 3 Proxy level psion.<br /> <br /> What you saying is that a Mesmerist can never learn powers as a Psiad? They don\u2019t follow the same rules at all.<br /> Same for Stalwarts can\u2019t they ever learn quantum powers no matter what they do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T05:56:37-07:00","id":1332111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332109#post1332109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you mean a Stalwart cannot train to became a Nova and a Mesmerist cannot train became a Psiad?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, correct.<br /> <br /> Who knows what will happen in 2e? It hasn\u2019t happened yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332109#post1332109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you saying is that a Mesmerist can never learn powers as a Psiad? They don\u2019t follow the same rules at all. Same for Stalwarts can\u2019t they ever learn quantum powers no matter what they do?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, correct. They *literally* did not follow the same rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 08-22-2019, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T06:11:12-07:00","id":1332112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332111#post1332111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 1e, correct.<br /> <br /> Who knows what will happen in 2e? It hasn\u2019t happened yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In 1e, correct. They *literally* did not follow the same rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I always thought that The rules in Adventure were for Limiting the evolution. I know there is an E-book dealing with Mesmerists / Stalwarts as a intermediate of Psiads / Novas and Daredevils, but it was not an oficial book and it was causing a lot of discussion on the Eon (back then).<br /> <br /> Ok... I guess my reality in the Continuum is a bit more different than I used to think...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T10:37:48-07:00","id":1332150,"title":"","content":"If Mesmerists and Stalwarts remain distinct from Psiads and low-Quantum Novas (as I assume they will since they need to be tailored to the themes and genre motifs of Adventure!), one interesting issue that rises then is their power balance with Talents.<br /> <br /> Since Psiads are supposed to non-diagetically on par with Talents (diagetically Dramatic Editing isn\u2019t perceivable even by the wielded, but for gameplay purposes it gives a massive edge balancing Talents with other Tier 2 characters with overt power sets) - and Mesmerists are weaker than Psiads, that creates the issue of whether \u201cDaredevils\u201d will outclass Mesmerists and Stalwarts.<br /> <br /> Of course in 1e Mesmerists and Stalwarts could also use Dramatic Editing, and that could easily make up the difference for Mesmerist psychic powers being weaker than Psiads and Stalwarts super attributes putting them behind Superiors - but given the desire to play up the distinctions in the power sets this edition i\u2019m guessing they won\u2019t go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T11:30:21-07:00","id":1332154,"title":"","content":"I would say that Mesmerists and Stalwarts are weaker than Psiads and Novas, but they have Dramatic Editing as an advantage that is enough to balance everything.<br /> <br /> I am really curious to see how the Superiors will work... I don\u2019t think they are dramatic editors, but...<br /> <br /> If we follow the Awaiting Inspiration definitions (the e-book I mentioned), you have Stalwarts and Mesmerists handling Teluric Energy (a mix of Quantum and Noetic) with more emphasis to one side or the other, while Daredevils are just balance between them and a more subconscious control than the others.<br /> <br /> The problem there is that on 1e there was no \u201cother energy\u201d handled by the Daredevils, while on 2e the Talents have some control over Flux, the interdimentional energy. That would create a 6th kind of character a that handle pure Flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-22-2019, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T12:00:54-07:00","id":1332162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332154#post1332154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would create a 6th kind of character a that handle pure Flux.</div> </div> </div> </div>Max Mercer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T12:06:31-07:00","id":1332164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332162#post1332162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Max Mercer.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, Mercer would be one of them, but they would lose some of the Talent capacities that are \u201cteluric\u201d by essence, probably Dramatic Editing.<br /> <br /> <br /> by the way, Excelsior... good name for Tier 3 Talent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-22-2019, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T12:11:05-07:00","id":1332165,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify - The idea of Telluric energy wasn\u2019t that it was actually a mix that was somehow different from pure Noetic or pure Quantum - it\u2019s just in the 1920s the Aron society hadn\u2019t figured out the distinction yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T13:28:10-07:00","id":1332177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332165#post1332165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify - The idea of Telluric energy wasn\u2019t that it was actually a mix that was somehow different from pure Noetic or pure Quantum - it\u2019s just in the 1920s the Aron society hadn\u2019t figured out the distinction yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that why I dont like the idea of Mesmerists and Stalwarts as different from the Psiads and Novas. The original explanation is... flawed to be honest. You can\u2019t be handling Quantum and Psi at the same time, that\u2019s the entire point of the corruption form Trinity, than you have Stalwarts that are handling both but a little more to the Quantum side, and Mesmerists a bit to the Psi side, and Daredevils right in the middle, and at same time they are not handling anything because there is no 3rd source. Of course it\u2019s all 1e...<br /> <br /> TC: we didn\u2019t see anything yet, so let\u2019s wait for the explanations to Psiads and Superiors...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T14:04:23-07:00","id":1332184,"title":"","content":"Sooooo I really what Superiors and Psiads (In no particular order of want, I want them both equally). <br /> <br /> Among the many reasons that I want them one of the main ones is that I am not a super fan of Psions due to the whole alien making them thing. But Psiads are natural. <br /> <br /> Also, I really want them so that I could make a modified scifi setting where the powers that be are either Psaids or Superiors, depending on which category suits my needs. <br /> <br /> That actually leads me to a question - when it comes to Adventure! sorts of people does anyone consider the division on powers more setting then mechanical. That is, anyone else think that if a player says &quot;I like Knack x but it only exists as a Mesmerist, can I have it even though I am a Stalwart.&quot; With the answer being YES, <br /> <br /> Anyway. on the topic at large. I am among the group that has Stalwarts/Superiors as lesser form Novas and Mesmermists as lesser form Psiads. They are closer to the shores which is why their power ability is a bit lesser than others. That said I am also of the camp that says given time and personal training and such one of the lesser can transform/transition into one of the greater. <br /> <br /> On that I add that for Stalwarts turning into Novas they gain certain Edges that reduce the risk and worry on gaining Flux due to their greater understanding of the energy of their power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T14:24:26-07:00","id":1332188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332177#post1332177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, that why I dont like the idea of Mesmerists and Stalwarts as different from the Psiads and Novas. The original explanation is... flawed to be honest. You can\u2019t be handling Quantum and Psi at the same time, that\u2019s the entire point of the corruption form Trinity, than you have Stalwarts that are handling both but a little more to the Quantum side, and Mesmerists a bit to the Psi side, and Daredevils right in the middle, and at same time they are not handling anything because there is no 3rd source. Of course it\u2019s all 1e...<br /> <br /> TC: we didn\u2019t see anything yet, so let\u2019s wait for the explanations to Psiads and Superiors...</div> </div> </div> </div>Handling the same power doesn\u2019t require they be the same thing. Mesmerized and Psiads channel the same energies - but Mesmerists are an earlier evolutionary step in wielder.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the difference between homo heidelbergensis and homo sapiens, not the difference between a child and an adult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T14:31:45-07:00","id":1332191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332188#post1332188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Handling the same power doesn\u2019t require they be the same thing. Mesmerized and Psiads channel the same energies - but Mesmerists are an earlier evolutionary step in wielder.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the difference between homo heidelbergensis and homo sapiens, not the difference between a child and an adult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the entire Awaiting Inspiration is not what is intended. Thank you!<br /> <br /> Still, a Stalwart could erupt to became a full Nova or once &quot;erupted&quot; to Stalwart you are locked on it? I guess they are locked by the way you are dealing with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T14:53:49-07:00","id":1332194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332184#post1332184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That actually leads me to a question - when it comes to Adventure! sorts of people does anyone consider the division on powers more setting then mechanical. That is, anyone else think that if a player says &quot;I like Knack x but it only exists as a Mesmerist, can I have it even though I am a Stalwart.&quot; With the answer being YES,</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Stalwart is not capable of turning into a full nova and a Mesmerist is not capable of turning into a Psiad, its out of limits because they don't work on the same rules...<br /> <br /> BUT... if there is the possibility of evolution in the same energy usage, a Stalwart with Flame Conjuration is just the Quantum Attack power and a Mesmerist with Aetheric Vision is just Sense Spectrum EK base power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332184#post1332184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway. on the topic at large. I am among the group that has Stalwarts/Superiors as lesser form Novas and Mesmermists as lesser form Psiads. They are closer to the shores which is why their power ability is a bit lesser than others. That said I am also of the camp that says given time and personal training and such one of the lesser can transform/transition into one of the greater.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stalwarts are different from Superiors, the same way a Psiad is different from a Psion, its a forced evolution, so I not counting here, they are locked on their condition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T14:54:25-07:00","id":1332195,"title":"","content":"The way I see it is that Stalwarts/Mesmerists would need a second kickstart to evolve into the higher nova/psiad power form. It will never happen on its own, it needs someone like Mal or Bhurano to build and activate a Quantum/psi pulse bomb that smashes their energies across the world and boosts the larval stages into their evolved form. These things aren\u2019t simple to build, either. It took Mal And Bhurano decades/centuries to figure out.<br /> <br /> Hammersmith\u2019s event was unique and very special because it somehow exploded Flux, Quantum and Psi potential across the world. Paradoxically (possibly because of the conflicting energies) it couldn\u2019t trigger everyone to the higher state like later efforts. Those closest to it - Max, Mal, Bhurano and others - went immediately to the higher state. Those further away with potential activated into the lower state. Some rarer individuals across the world and times already had higher potential and triggered into (Probably the lowest power versions of) the higher state. Few of these individuals understood or noticed any difference between themselves and the others for some time. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> put it well in the evolutionary terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T15:10:53-07:00","id":1332198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332195#post1332195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it is that Stalwarts/Mesmerists would need a second kickstart to evolve into the higher nova/psiad power form. It will never happen on its own, it needs someone like Mal or Bhurano to build and activate a Quantum/psi pulse bomb that smashes their energies across the world and boosts the larval stages into their evolved form. These things aren\u2019t simple to build, either. It took Mal And Bhurano decades/centuries to figure out.<br /> <br /> Hammersmith\u2019s event was unique and very special because it somehow exploded Flux, Quantum and Psi potential across the world. Paradoxically (possibly because of the conflicting energies) it couldn\u2019t trigger everyone to the higher state like later efforts. Those closest to it - Max, Mal, Bhurano and others - went immediately to the higher state. Those further away with potential activated into the lower state. Some rarer individuals across the world and times already had higher potential and triggered into (Probably the lowest power versions of) the higher state. Few of these individuals understood or noticed any difference between themselves and the others for some time.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> put it well in the evolutionary terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the way you are describing. It is like a half way activation, you can do some stuff but can't go as far as the ones that were activated all the way.<br /> <br /> It also allow some of the Stalwarts that survived until 2018 to became full novas, and even guys like Pax can possibly be kicked from Stalwarts to Novas in the process (maybe a small eruption). The same could happen later, with some Mesmerists becoming Psiads in 2104.<br /> <br /> The same way as other people Erupting, it could probably happen much after the event that started it, or even without a proper event but a rare condition, just like the Psiads that are around in the Aberrant Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T16:24:18-07:00","id":1332204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332191#post1332191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then the entire Awaiting Inspiration is not what is intended. Thank you!<br /> <br /> Still, a Stalwart could erupt to became a full Nova or once &quot;erupted&quot; to Stalwart you are locked on it? I guess they are locked by the way you are dealing with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A secondary evolution ala the first jump from baseline would be feasible, just saying it is such a jump rather than just a gradual stat acquisition.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve considered the possibility of presenting Primoris as a powerful Stalwart who makes the jump to Nova after he and Mercer are caught in the Trinity blast in \u201845 (Mercer for his part gets thrown through time)<br /> <br /> Might do the same with Pax, have him have initially been a Stalwart, who erupted to Nova with N-Day.<br /> <br /> But i\u2019ll decide when we see 2e Adventure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-22-2019, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T22:34:43-07:00","id":1332233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332092#post1332092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psiads have been around since at least the Hammersmith incident*. Bhurano was the most powerful (much like Michael and Max were the most powerful of their type) but they were pre-Galatea.<br /> <br /> * Since the Hammersmith explosion echoed back and forwards in time (in 1st edition, at least), from the moment of the explosion psiads were around before it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there were Mesmerists and Psiads coexisting during the Adventure! period. Did Stalwarts and Mesmerists exist in other time periods, or just during Adventure!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T12:39:17-07:00","id":1332362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332233#post1332233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So there were Mesmerists and Psiads coexisting during the Adventure! period. Did Stalwarts and Mesmerists exist in other time periods, or just during Adventure!?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as we know NEW ONES don\u2019t keep happening as the stronger evolutionary strain takes hold, but Whitney Styles hangs around, so unless he had a secondary evolution, there\u2019s one Mesmerist.<br /> <br /> Also I suspect Aeon era Superiors might look a lot like Stalwarts, but I could be wrong about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T14:08:22-07:00","id":1332366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328407-spoilers-aberrant-setting-changes?p=1332362#post1332362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as we know NEW ONES don\u2019t keep happening as the stronger evolutionary strain takes hold, but Whitney Styles hangs around, so unless he had a secondary evolution, there\u2019s one Mesmerist.<br /> <br /> Also I suspect Aeon era Superiors might look a lot like Stalwarts, but I could be wrong about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible that Whitney were a Psiad since beginning, I mean, he is described as a &quot;Mesmerist with High Inspiration&quot;. Or maybe he evolved to a Psiad later, as Mesmerists don't usually have extended lifespan (as far as I recall).<br /> <br /> My bet on Superiors is on restricted Nova (much like a Psion have restrictions over Psiads). Of course it would follow the rules from Aeon, what means not a big use of scales and very limited powers. Seeing by another side, a Superior could have &quot;Gifts&quot; in place of Mega Attributes and Mega Edges, as they are already defined in Core... well... lets see... a few more weeks probably...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://f